CAT = "zare5KeyInd"; SEG = "KEY"
Q = [
("Under the FAIS Act, a key individual is a person who:",
 "Manages or oversees the services", ["Advises the largest number of clients", "Owns the most shares in the FSP", "Audits the FSP's annual accounts"],
 "A key individual manages or oversees, alone or with others, the activities of the FSP relating to rendering financial services. Ownership or sales volume does not make someone a key individual."),
("Before a person acts as an FSP's key individual, who must approve them?",
 "The Authority", ["The FSP's board alone", "The compliance officer", "The Ombud for FSPs"],
 "A key individual must be approved by the Authority, which checks that the person meets the fit and proper requirements."),
("A sole proprietor FSP has no staff. Its key individual is:",
 "The sole proprietor", ["Not required at all", "An outside person it must hire", "The product supplier's manager"],
 "A sole proprietor manages and oversees its own financial services, so the sole proprietor is also the key individual."),
("Which requirements must a key individual meet?",
 "Honesty, integrity, competence", ["Only a postgraduate degree", "Only five years of sales experience", "Only a clean credit record"],
 "Key individuals must meet the fit and proper requirements: honesty, integrity and good standing, competence (experience, qualifications, exams, CPD) and, where applicable, financial soundness."),
("A key individual's main responsibility towards the representatives is to:",
 "Oversee the services given", ["Pay their commission personally", "Write their regulatory exams", "Prepare their tax returns"],
 "Key individuals are responsible for managing and overseeing the rendering of financial services, including by representatives, so that it complies with the Act."),
("A key individual no longer meets the honesty and integrity requirements. The FSP must:",
 "Stop them acting as key individual", ["Keep them on until licence renewal", "Move them into an advice role", "Inform clients only on request"],
 "A person who fails the honesty and integrity requirement may not act as a key individual (or as a representative), so the FSP must remove them and inform the Authority."),
("An FSP's only key individual is no longer fit and proper and has not been replaced. What may happen?",
 "The FSP's licence may be suspended", ["Nothing, if the reps are qualified", "The Ombud takes over the FSP", "A representative becomes key individual"],
 "An FSP must have an approved key individual for each category it is licensed for. Without one it no longer meets the licence requirements, and the Authority may suspend the licence, which stops its representatives too."),
("Which of these is a regulated responsibility of a key individual?",
 "Ensuring representatives are competent", ["Approving clients' claims at the insurer", "Setting product suppliers' premiums", "Deciding complaints at the Ombud"],
 "Key individuals oversee the FSP's financial services, which includes making sure representatives meet the fit and proper requirements and are supervised where needed."),
("A key individual is approved to oversee:",
 "Particular classes of business", ["Every class automatically", "Only Category I business", "Only one product supplier"],
 "BN 194 of 2017 links a key individual's approval to the classes of business they manage or oversee, and requires class of business training for each before they do so."),
("May a key individual also act as a representative of the same FSP?",
 "Yes, if fit for both roles", ["No, the FAIS Act prohibits it", "Only for three months", "Only for Category IV business"],
 "A person may be both a key individual and a representative, provided they meet the fit and proper requirements for each role."),
("Who must keep the FSP's internal register of its key individuals and representatives?",
 "The FSP", ["The Ombud for FSPs", "Each product supplier", "The Financial Intelligence Centre"],
 "The FSP maintains a register of its representatives and key individuals and keeps it up to date, while the Authority keeps a central register."),
("How does a key individual keep their knowledge current after approval?",
 "Ongoing professional development", ["Rewriting the RE1 every year", "A new degree every five years", "An annual polygraph test at the FSCA"],
 "Key individuals, like representatives, must complete continuous professional development (CPD) activities in each CPD cycle."),
]
